CORE
main.ii
--winx64 --cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ bit cast: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ round trip: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
__builtin_bit_cast was a keyword in GCC and clang modes only; in Visual
Studio mode it was an unknown symbol, and the MSVC STL's _Bit_cast lost its
body (44 cbmc-cpp failures on VS 2022).  Preprocessed, as cbmc on Linux
would otherwise use the host's (GNU) preprocessor.
